WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:03.290
25 October 1854.

2
00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:08.150
A valley in the Crimean War,
with Russian guns on three sides.

3
00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:11.440
A confused order passes from hand to hand.

4
00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:14.330
And the Light Brigade rides
straight down the middle.

5
00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:17.580
Tennyson's poem gallops
after them: "Half a league,

6
00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:21.410
half a league," and
"Rode the six hundred."

7
00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.730
He admits someone blundered.

8
00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:27.330
Yet his last stanza
orders us: Honour them.

9
00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:30.550
If the charge was a
mistake, why honour it?

10
00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:34.890
In this mission, you'll find out how one
confused order sent the brigade at the

11
00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:35.920
guns.

12
00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:40.970
You'll feel the poem's galloping rhythm:
two beats to a line, like hooves.

13
00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:44.760
And you'll track a refrain that
changes as the charge goes on.

14
00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:48.350
Your mission: explain why
the poem says 'Honour'.
